{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/800710-touchstones-bonds-in-2e","id":800710,"title":"Touchstones/Bonds in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T13:36:05-08:00","id":800710,"title":"Touchstones/Bonds in 2e","content":"I've had the new Delta Green on the brain lately, and one of the subsystems added in the new edition is Bonds; ratings for the relationships with the people outside of the job that help keep you sane. You can draw upon your Bonds to help you with Sanity rolls, at cost to the health of that particular relationship (so you don't have a panic attack when the other guy in your cell gets his head blown off, but then you're understandably distant with your husband the next time you see him).<br /> <br /> I feel like it's a cool enough concept to consider stealing for Hunter, especially in games that emphasize the personal cost of the Vigil (which I hope the Slasher Chronicle does), and there's an existing similar mechanic in the Touchstones of Vampire 2e. <br /> <br /> Thoughts on something like this, or is it too grim for Hunter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:53:23-08:00","id":800721,"title":"","content":"I would imagine Hunters <i>need </i>additional Anchors to keep doing what they do, both mechanically and narratively since they still use Integrity. I would guess that whatever form it takes, it will tie into the ability to maintain your Integrity despite regularly encountering things that risk it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:31:58-08:00","id":800803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/800710-touchstones-bonds-in-2e#post800710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had the new Delta Green on the brain lately, and one of the subsystems added in the new edition is Bonds; ratings for the relationships with the people outside of the job that help keep you sane. You can draw upon your Bonds to help you with Sanity rolls, at cost to the health of that particular relationship (so you don't have a panic attack when the other guy in your cell gets his head blown off, but then you're understandably distant with your husband the next time you see him).<br /> <br /> I feel like it's a cool enough concept to consider stealing for Hunter, especially in games that emphasize the personal cost of the Vigil (which I hope the Slasher Chronicle does), and there's an existing similar mechanic in the Touchstones of Vampire 2e.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on something like this, or is it too grim for Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very similar to something I'm doing in my home game of CofD meets Burn Notice. And it's not actually been very grim thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T22:30:38-08:00","id":801098,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see what you have sketched out for that mechanically, if you're willing to share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T04:31:16-08:00","id":801277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/800710-touchstones-bonds-in-2e#post800710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View 